Overlay patch 0022 (rev10):
rev9: eviction runs on ALL ImportTexture exits — PNG pack textures take the
LOAD_AS_IMG early return, so the tail block NEVER ran for exactly the
textures the budget exists to bound. Tail is now a lambda called on all
three exits. (Every prior forced-pressure sim test was a no-op; device
budget behavior was actually the upstream count cap.)
rev8: eviction floor (128 entries) is now cvar gSohIos.TexCacheMinEntries —
sim tracks sit under 128 entries so every forced-pressure sim test was a
silent no-op. byte-budget texture cache (reference 0020 rev2).
rev7: budget back to 1280 — 1024 thrashes the 4K working set (sprite/tree
blink, user-observed on device); the rev6 valve owns burst safety now.
rev6: footprint panic valve — phys_footprint > gSohIos.MemPanicMB (default
2900) during an import storm cuts the ledger to half budget. The ledger
model under-counts bursts (un-imported resources, decode buffers,
allocator lag): 3.2 GB observed live at ledger budget 1024.
rev5: 1280 -> 1024 (bursts overshoot ~+600MB over steady; device-measured).
rev4: iPhone default budget 1536 -> 1280 (rev3-semantics memory math; see inline).
rev3: budget eviction also unloads the CPU-side resource (coupled with
0030, which adds TextureCacheValue::resource_path — compile-coupled pair).
rev2: DeleteTexture subtract is mip-aware (+1/3 for 0021 rev3+ chains).
Original (reference 0020 = SYNC
WAVE 1 mandatory fix 5; anchors byte-identical at our pin). Fast3D's cache
is COUNT-based and Metal's DeleteTexture was EMPTY — eviction never freed
GPU memory, so big packs pin gigabytes and jetsam at menu upload bursts.
1. gfx_rendering_api.h: virtual GetTextureBytes() (default 0 disables the
   budget on other backends).
2. Metal: DeleteTexture actually releases + exact ledger (mTextureBytes,
   fed by 0021's UploadTexture accounting).
3. interpreter.cpp ImportTexture tail (__IOS__): LRU-evict to
   gSohIos.TexCacheBudgetMB (default 1536), floor 128 entries.
Sole pin delta vs the Ship of Harkinian port patch: Context::GetInstance (pre-rename).

